{number: 51}
{title: I Am Thine, O Lord}
{key: Ab}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Ab] I am Thine, O Lord, I have [Db] heard Thy voice,
And it [Ab] told Thy love to [Eb7] me;
But I [Ab] long to rise in the [Db] arms of faith,
And be [Ab] closer [Eb7] drawn to [Ab] Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Draw me [Ab] nearer, nearer, blessed [Db] Lord,
To the [Ab] cross where Thou hast [Eb7] died;
Draw me [Ab] nearer, nearer, nearer, [Db] blessed Lord,
To Thy [Ab] precious, [Eb7] bleeding [Ab] side.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Ab] Consecrate me now to Thy [Db] service, Lord,
By the [Ab] pow'r of grace di-[Eb7] vine;
Let my [Ab] soul look up with a [Db] steadfast hope,
And my [Ab] will be [Eb7] lost in [Ab] Thine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
O the [Ab] pure delight of a [Db] single hour
That be-[Ab] fore Thy throne I [Eb7] spend;
When I [Ab] kneel in prayer, and with [Db] Thee, my God,
I com-[Ab] mune as [Eb7] friend with [Ab] friend!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
There are [Ab] depths of love that I [Db] cannot know
Till I [Ab] cross the narrow [Eb7] sea;
There are [Ab] heights of joy that I [Db] may not reach
Till I [Ab] rest in [Eb7] peace with [Ab] Thee.
{end_of_verse}
